      {
        "id": 97471,
        "name": "Ironic",
        "username": "Ironic",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ironic/{size}/2171_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-04-03T03:50:22.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Hurm - a group of metahumans worshipping a sun-themed being in the Sentinels universe. &nbsp;Sounds legit.</p>\n<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Foote\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/48/1877_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Foote:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p><b>Silverleaf wrote:</b></p>\n<div><blockquote>My friend can deadlift 90kg. She weighs 60kg, and looks like she might break if you look at her too hard. I try not to annoy her...\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote></div>\nSpeak American please<span>\n</span></blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>\"My friend can lift one and a half times her body weight despite looking frail, and is even capable of using simple internet searches to find unit conversions.\"</p>\n<p>And, sure, not everyone who is incredible shape looks bulky and muscular - I am always struck when I look at UFC champions that even the <a href=\"http://www.mtv.com/onair/bully_beatdown/seaons2/images/flipbooks/fighters/tony_lopez/crops/5290.jpg\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">high-weight</a> <a href=\"http://i4.photobucket.com/albums/y141/gregwapling/tv/ufc/profiles/cain-velasquez-body.png\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">male</a> <a href=\"http://www.sherdog.com/thumbnail_crop.php?image=http://www.cdn.sherdog.com/_images/pictures/20090123061659_IMG_8020.JPG&amp;&amp;width_size=600\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">champs</a> aren't built like weightlifters - they wind up chiseled, but since fighting is generally pretty anaerobic and a lot of musclemass can slow you down (fighting is fairly rarely about strength past a certain point, really), they look more like a tough person you'd see on the street than a spandex-clad colossus. &nbsp;And, of course, some of the lighter female champs look like actors I'd call out as miscast if they were portrayed as professional martial artists in a movie, since <a href=\"http://www.girlswithmuscle.com/images/full/746549258.jpg\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">little musclemass at all can be seen</a>.</p>\n<p>So, sure, your point is well taken. &nbsp;And larger discussion of superhero body image portrayals is really a tediusly dull debate I'm sure we've all had at least as many times as we're interested in. &nbsp;The most important thing is the information we already have: that Pauline is just as super-strong as Paul - no more, no less.</p>",
