      {
        "id": 97473,
        "name": "Reckless",
        "username": "Reckless",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/reckless/{size}/2467_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-04-05T07:24:33.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Katsue\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/katsue/48/2012_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Katsue:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div><b>Reckless wrote:</b><br><blockquote>&nbsp;But something may have happened to the Legacy line by the time GSF happens?&nbsp; Rough...\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote></div>\nNot necessarily. If America ceased to exist for whatever reason any Legacies running around might end up being depowered.\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p><br>That may be true.&nbsp; I just know that the Legacy family is known to have a decent bit of tragedy surrounding them.&nbsp; Dead parents, dead children, oppressive dictators, etc.&nbsp; This was averted according to what we've learned in the Tactics Kickstarter and I'm wondering if Legacy isn't overdue for a little more trauma in his family's lives.</p>",
