      {
        "id": 97474,
        "name": "TheSoundOfTrees",
        "username": "TheSoundOfTrees",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/t/da6949/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2014-04-07T11:47:33.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Christopher\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/christopher/48/1851_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Christopher:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<blockquote>\nSo, is it safe to assume that, far in the future setting of GSF, after many generations of Legacies, that the current Legacy is a deity?\n</blockquote>\nUnless something were to happen...\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Hold on, hold on. New completely false theory incoming.</p>\n<p>Unknown Cosmic Entity Or Equivalent needs a body. Sends a seed of power to earth. It implants in a man, giving him small powers - but his first child shows the same abilities, and adds a new one. It takes generations, but at last, the \"body\" is ready, at full power - or powerful enough to be of use to UnkCosEntOrEquiv. This is the famous \"Child\" we are wondering about elsewhere. The Legacy line is slowly nurtured to become the body of a powerful entity.</p>\n<p>So Pauline is the child. Or maybe the potential mother of the Child.</p>\n<p>Completely false, I don't doubt it.</p>\n<p>I can't wait to see what Christopher has in store for the End of the Legacy Line.</p>",
